<aside class="research-callout" aria-label="FDD external research">
  <span class="eyebrow">INDEPENDENT RESEARCH / THE AIA SECURITY MODEL</span>
  <h3 class="research-statement">Even unlimited time and computing power cannot recover protected information when the required information is unavailable.</h3>
  <p class="research-attribution"><strong>FDD Transformative Cyber Innovation Lab</strong><br/><cite>“Protecting and Securing Data from the Quantum Threat”</cite> — 2022<br/><span>Research conclusion, summarized</span></p>
  <p>The AIA model evaluated with Cyber Reliant applies information-theoretic security by fragmenting and distributing the information required for reconstruction, including protected data and cryptographic components. More computing power alone cannot recreate missing required information.</p>
  <a class="text-link" href={source}>Read the FDD research <Arrow/></a>
  <p class="research-boundary">Research relates to the evaluated AIA approach and should not be interpreted as certification of every Cyber Reliant product implementation.</p>
</aside>
